    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense faces a favorable slate today, anchored by **Kyle Tucker** (85.72) and **Andy Pages** (75.64). Both players benefit significantly from a prime matchup against Sugano; the combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and the pitcher\u2019s high xERA allows these two to anchor our production. **Drake Baldwin** (72.68) remains a high-floor play in the leadoff spot, bolstered by a 5% wind-out advantage and a soft matchup against Ober. While **Jacob Wilson** (61.21) is another reliable start, we are closely monitoring the lineups for **Gunnar Henderson**, **Coby Mayo**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Andy Pages** to ensure our projections align with their confirmed placements; a shift lower in the order for any of these hitters would require a reassessment of their daily efficiency scores.\n\nThe decision to keep **Sam Antonacci** on the bench (39.73) was the most difficult call of the day, as he fell just shy of our 40.0 efficiency floor. While his base projections were respectable, a platoon disadvantage against Imanaga and a lower projected spot in the batting order pushed him into the \"below floor\" category, prioritizing the optimization of our SB and power ceilings elsewhere. Conversely, we must exercise caution with **Gunnar Henderson**, whose matchup against McClanahan is the most challenging of the day; his dynamic platoon disadvantage (-15%) suppressed his score to 53.52, making him a marginal start that we are holding in the lineup purely for his high base ceiling. With **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** unavailable, our depth\u2014including bench options like **Nasim Nunez**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, **Curtis Mead**, **Dominic Smith**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Luis Lara**\u2014will be on standby should any last-minute lineup changes occur or if we need to pinch-hit for a struggling bat.",
